{"agent":"pf2-kilo","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `runs_window_days` knob is registered under a new `metrics_runs` section, but the stated change contract says the window is configured as `[metrics].runs_window_days`. Given an operator config file containing:\n\n```toml\n[metrics]\nruns_window_days = 7\n```\n\nthis `MetricsRunsConfig` will not bind that value because it declares the section as `metrics_runs`; the runs report will therefore keep using the default 30-day window even though the operator set the documented `[metrics]` knob.","digest":"bfb596f935b8a8c8","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/config_sections/metrics_runs.py:17","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/config_sections/metrics_runs.py:17"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`provider` ignores `[metrics].min_samples`, so it can emit non-`None` headline rates from an insufficient sample. For example, with `cfg.metrics.min_samples = 5` and exactly one merged item that passed first time, `provider` returns `runs.first_pass_rate = 1.0`, `runs.runs_per_merge = 1.0`, and `runs.total_runs = 1`. The module contract says a figure with fewer than `min_samples` merged items is `None`/unavailable, and `rollup` enforces this via `_rate`; the provider does not, so `ddflow metrics`/MCP/brief can display 100% first-pass from a single item.","digest":"1036b426e81b1325","family":"alibaba","location":"`provider` (ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py)","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"`provider` (ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py)"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The `group_by` knob is inert: it is validated and echoed, but it does not change any computed rollup. Given identical `events`, `state`, `cfg`, `now`, `phase`, and `since`, calls with `group_by=\"phase\"` and `group_by=\"gate\"` return the same `per_phase`, `per_model`, and `per_gate` data; only the `group_by` field differs. If a caller relies on the documented grouping knob to change the report output, it will not.","digest":"98a383b1e7770b84","family":"alibaba","location":"`rollup` (ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py)","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"`rollup` (ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py)"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test named `test_a_review_gate_is_labelled_a_model_gate_and_others_deterministic` does not actually exercise a model/review gate. It only creates the deterministic `unit_tests` gate and asserts that its `gate_kind` is `\"deterministic\"`. If `runs_to_merge` mislabels every gate as deterministic, including review/model gates, this test still passes. The acceptance explicitly requires deterministic and model gates to be labelled separately, so the fixture should include a review gate event and assert something like `gate_kind == \"model\"`; without that input, the test fails to cover the required separation.","digest":"c64570a9e6c10ee9","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py:95-98","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py:95-98"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The `runs_window_days` configuration knob is not tested for its actual effect. The test sets `cfg.metrics_runs.runs_window_days = 30` and only asserts that the returned report echoes `window.days == 30`. A `rollup` implementation that ignores `cfg.metrics_runs.runs_window_days` and always includes all events would still pass. The acceptance says the window knob changes the output; a concrete missing case is setting `runs_window_days` small enough to exclude fixture items and asserting that `merged`/`per_item` changes accordingly.","digest":"da8260dfe8f342b9","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py:81-84","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py:81-84"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The acceptance fixture needs a per-item first-pass rate of passes/runs (1/1 → 100% and 1/3 → 33%) beside run counts 1 and 3. `_per_item` stores `first_pass` as the boolean `not failed and not weak`, and `rollup`’s `first_pass_rate` is the share of items with that flag. On that fixture the boolean report is True vs False and the headline rate is 1/2 = 50%; no field is 0.33. `passes` and `runs` are raw counts only, so the required percentages are never emitted.","digest":"824a9f7dbfc33014","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:_per_item","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:_per_item"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The module contract says a figure with fewer than `[metrics].min_samples` merged items is None, and `rollup` implements that via `_rate`. `provider` does not: with `min_samples=5` and one merged item that passed, it emits `runs.first_pass_rate` = 1.0 (and `runs.runs_per_merge` = 1.0) instead of None. Headline MCP/brief rows therefore disagree with `rollup` on the same log.","digest":"042f56b4315fe87e","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:provider","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:provider"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`group_by` is validated and copied into the result, but it does not select or reshape any figure. `per_phase`, `per_model`, and `per_gate` are always fully computed; there is no `rollups` key. `rollup(..., group_by=\"phase\")` and `rollup(..., group_by=\"model\")` on the same events differ only in the echoed string, so the grouping knob does not change the report the docstring and acceptance say it changes.","digest":"97efa492fb13a382","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:rollup","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:rollup"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":17013,"diff_sha":"708270aa1b407c379d4a7bacaaa69fc4d3a2a88dcca2a40a83807ea89c285fb8","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PM-runs-to-merge","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":104.6,"excluded_bytes":1296,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":8,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"1cf30c08275e23a0","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PM-runs-to-merge.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261112T001733Z-b9cb4879.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794442653.1678195,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"4689fab65b72fe291a7839c93c91b5390ac0e75d","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/config_sections/metrics_runs.py":"100644 b79be3b141ca689261ae531fcb4268fc79c3fae8","ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py":"100644 90007dfcef5375da89f51d961f7816b13966366d","ddflow/services/metrics/service.py":"100644 63440165bf890b6c72d1c184b481450e18f11cf1","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr":"100644 0e58c0e8ea87118c82d84757f8f6509ebd6ebd66","tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py":"100644 c4dea4fa140da110d12976c0fc247837499b255f"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/config_sections/metrics_runs.py:17","`provider` (ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py)","`rollup` (ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py)","tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py:95-98","tests/test_metrics_runs_to_merge.py:81-84","ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:_per_item","ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:provider","ddflow/services/metrics/runs_to_merge.py:rollup"],"tree_sha":"4689fab65b72+cl